@archive @publication
Feature: Publish log archives to object storage
  Operators can retain accepted logs in the archive while querying them locally.

  Scenario: Publish an acknowledged log export and reclaim its staging file
    Given log archival is configured for a disposable object store
    When the service accepts and publishes a log export
    Then the object store should contain one Parquet batch with the accepted logs
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed
    And the acknowledged logs should still be queryable locally

  Scenario: Recover a committed upload after its acknowledgement is lost
    Given an acknowledged log batch staged with a different Parquet encoding
    When the service restarts after the object store commits an unacknowledged upload and staging is lost
    Then the original archive object should remain unchanged
    And the object store should contain one Parquet batch with the accepted logs
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed
    And the acknowledged logs should still be queryable locally

  Scenario: Enable publication for a database that already contains staged logs
    Given a log batch staged on the previous database schema
    When the upgraded service publishes the staged batch
    Then the original batch identity and membership should be preserved
    And the object store should contain one Parquet batch with the accepted logs
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed

  Scenario: Resume archive publication after stopping during a multipart upload
    Given an acknowledged log batch staged for multipart upload
    When the service stops during a multipart upload and restarts
    Then the unfinished upload should be aborted while the staged batch remains available
    And the object store should contain one Parquet batch with the accepted logs
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed
    And the acknowledged logs should still be queryable locally

  Scenario: Recheck the archive after a multipart upload fails to start
    Given an acknowledged log batch staged for multipart upload
    When the object store temporarily rejects the start of the multipart upload
    Then the worker should check the object before starting another multipart upload
    And the object store should contain one Parquet batch with the accepted logs
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed

  Scenario: Recover a multipart upload when the completion acknowledgement is lost
    Given an acknowledged log batch staged for multipart upload
    When the service restarts after the object store commits an unacknowledged upload and staging is lost
    Then the original archive object should remain unchanged
    And the object store should contain one Parquet batch with the accepted logs
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed
    And the acknowledged logs should still be queryable locally

  Scenario: Preserve staging when the verification download fails its checksum
    Given log archival is configured for a disposable object store
    When the store serves different bytes during verification and then serves the correct object
    Then the batch should have stayed unconfirmed with its staged file intact
    And the object store should contain one Parquet batch with the accepted logs
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed

  Scenario Outline: Preserve a competing object created during a multipart upload
    Given an acknowledged log batch staged for multipart upload
    When another writer creates the same key with different bytes and the "<metadata>" checksum before completion
    Then the competing object should still have its original bytes
    And the batch should have stayed unconfirmed with its staged file intact

    Examples:
      | metadata  |
      | competing |
      | attempted |

  Scenario: Recognize the original upload when it commits during a regenerated attempt
    Given an acknowledged log batch staged with a different Parquet encoding
    When the original upload commits as the restarted service tries to upload regenerated bytes
    Then the confirmed checksum should be the earlier of the two attempted checksums
    And the object store should contain one Parquet batch with the accepted logs
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed

  Scenario: Resume cleanup after a confirmed batch's staging directory becomes writable
    Given an acknowledged log batch staged with a different Parquet encoding
    When staging cleanup fails and the service restarts after write access returns
    Then the batch should have stayed confirmed with its staged file intact
    And the original archive object should remain unchanged
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed

  Scenario: Reconcile an existing archive while restaging is blocked
    Given an acknowledged log batch staged with a different Parquet encoding
    When the service restarts after an unacknowledged commit and cannot recreate the lost staged file
    Then the existing archive should be confirmed despite the failed restaging
    And the original archive object should remain unchanged
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed

  Scenario: Retry cleanup of a corrupt staged file after reconciling the remote object
    Given an acknowledged log batch staged with a different Parquet encoding
    When startup reconciles an unacknowledged upload while removal of its corrupt staged file is blocked
    Then the corrupt staged file should have remained pending for cleanup after confirmation
    And the original archive object should remain unchanged
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed

  Scenario: Reconcile an existing archive when the staged file cannot be read
    Given an acknowledged log batch staged with a different Parquet encoding
    When the service restarts after an unacknowledged commit with the staged file still unreadable
    Then the original archive object should remain unchanged
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed
    And the acknowledged logs should still be queryable locally

  Scenario: Regenerate corrupt staging while publication is running
    Given log archival is configured for a disposable object store
    When the staged file is corrupted during a store outage and access returns
    Then the batch should be published under its original archive key
    And the object store should contain one Parquet batch with the accepted logs
    And the published batch should be recorded and its staging file reclaimed

  Scenario: Reconcile a later committed batch while an earlier upload is missing
    Given acknowledged log batches are staged for two archive days
    When the service starts with an unreadable staged batch and only the later upload committed
    Then the earlier batch should remain unconfirmed and the later batch should be reclaimed

  Scenario: Continue publishing and evicting while cleanup of an earlier batch is blocked
    Given acknowledged log batches are staged for two archive days
    When the service publishes while the earlier staging directory is unwritable
    Then both batches should be confirmed and only the later batch should be reclaimed
    And eviction should reclaim the later batch and retain the earlier batch locally

  Scenario: Continue publication after upgrading a queue with blocked cleanup
    Given acknowledged log batches are staged for two archive days on the previous schema
    When the service publishes while the earlier staging directory is unwritable
    Then both batches should be confirmed and only the later batch should be reclaimed
    And publication should complete the healthy batch before retrying the blocked one
    And eviction should reclaim the later batch and retain the earlier batch locally

  Scenario: Publish newly accepted logs while repair of an earlier batch is blocked
    Given an acknowledged log export staged in Parquet
    When a staged file is corrupted and its directory is unwritable as logs arrive for another day
    Then only the newly accepted logs should be published and the blocked staging file should remain
